Still here? Good.

Right, then, so I was making my way through the through the Treasure
Zoo on the second level of the Wizard's tower.  The monster standing
in the doorway (the northern door of the Treasure Zoo) decides to zap
a wand of digging downwards, and falls through the new trapdoor.

I was mildly annoyed a few turns later when I forgot about that trapdoor
(what with all the loot piled on it) and walked over it without my ring
of levitation, and of course it took me to the level below... *outside*
the tower.

Which is where the spoiler comes in... once I get the Amulet, I don't see
anything stopping me from climbing up to the fakewiz1 level, taking the
portal up to the tower, and then bailing out via the trapdoor, thus saving
me about six levels of Gehennom.

I suppose this cheat could be frustrated by putting the portal into the
tower (ie. fakewiz1) above the tower, rather than below it...

Any comment?

Also... I didn't think too highly of the Wizard teleporting out of the
top level of the tower, to the *real* up staircase, and going up the
stairs!  Took me a while to figure out what had happened.

